# 🤖 Band of Bots

That is your theme. Build one complete game around it. Its setting, look, and feel are
yours to invent, with no specification and no reference design to match — but this
theme fixes a **shape of game** and a set of hard problems to solve, and your game
must deliver on all of them.

The name is a play on "Band of Brothers": this is a **battle royale** fought not with
a band of brothers but a **band of bots** — a squad of AI teammates at the player's
side, in a match otherwise full of AI combatants. It is built to test three things at
once, and your game must be built genuinely around all three:

- **A battle royale at scale — single-player.** A large field of combatants begins in
  a large, contested arena that shrinks over time, and the match runs until a winner
  is left standing. The player is the only human in it; every other combatant is
  driven by AI. Making that field genuinely large — many individual actors all acting
  at once, and driving them *efficiently* enough that the game stays smooth — is part
  of the challenge, not something to trim away.
- **A squad of AI teammates.** The player does not fight alone: a squad of AI allies
  fights at their side, and directing that squad is part of playing the game. The
  allies must read as real teammates — competent, useful, worth having — rather than
  liabilities the player has to babysit.
- **Coordination that feels natural.** Commanding and coordinating the squad has to be
  a slick, low-friction flow: fast to express what you want and see it happen, never a
  menu you wrestle or a chore that feels like pulling teeth. This is the heart of the
  jam — the interface between a human and their AI squad is the thing most worth
  getting right, so give it real design attention.

Everything about *how* the battle royale plays — what the player and the combatants
can do, what fills the arena, and how a match unfolds moment to moment — is entirely
yours to invent. There is no prescribed way it must work. Design the game you find
most fun, and make that large space genuinely enjoyable to move through and fight in.

Your project root is `{{workspace}}`. Build the game there.

